
- The power consumption of the amplifier should be no larger than 75 μW.
- The DC gain of the amplifier should be at least 100 dB.
- The common-mode rejection ratio (CMRR) at DC should be at least 70 dB.
- The power supply rejection ratio (PSRR) should be at least 70 dB.
- The gain-bandwidth product (GBW) should be at least 2000000.0 Hz.
- The phase margin should be at least 30 degrees.
- The power supply noise rejection (PSRN) should be at least 80 dB.
